# ==============================================================================
#  .gitattributes - per-path overrides for how Git treats files in this repo
# ==============================================================================
#  This file lets you change Git's behaviour for specific paths. Each rule is:
#
#       <pattern>   <attr> <attr> ...
#
#  (a glob on the left, one or more attributes on the right).
#
#  There are currently NO active rules. The file is kept - deliberately - as a
#  documented placeholder so that next time you open it you remember what it is
#  for and how to switch a feature on. Uncomment an example below to use it.
#
#  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  1. Line endings - normalise so a Windows/WSL checkout can't inject CRLF:
#       * text=auto eol=lf          # store LF in the repo, check out native
#       *.sh  text eol=lf           # shell scripts must stay LF
#       *.bat text eol=crlf         # Windows batch files want CRLF
#
#  2. Force a path to be treated as binary (no diff, no EOL munging):
#       *.png binary
#       *.pdf binary
#
#  3. Custom MERGE driver - point a path at a driver defined in gitconfig
#     (a `[merge "<name>"]` section with a `driver = ...` command). This is the
#     mechanism a tool like a JSONL tracker uses for smart merges:
#       path/to/file.jsonl merge=<driver-name>
#
#  4. Custom DIFF driver / language-aware hunk headers:
#       *.md diff=markdown
#
#  5. Keep generated or vendored files out of GitHub language stats and diffs:
#       dist/**    linguist-generated
#       vendor/**  linguist-vendored
#
#  6. Exclude paths from `git archive` / release tarballs:
#       .github/  export-ignore
#       tests/    export-ignore
#
#  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Note: Git LFS normally writes `filter=lfs` rules here (via `git lfs track`),
#  but this setup configures LFS globally in ~/.gitconfig instead, so nothing
#  LFS-related needs to live in this file.
#
#  Reference: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes
# ==============================================================================
